                      (        forth.asm):02383         * Anton Ertl's forth-standard.org notes on +LOOP (2019-05-21 05:54:21):
                      (        forth.asm):02384         * "Note that the loop control parameters can be either signed or unsigned,
                      (        forth.asm):02385         * and +LOOP has to work for both. For systems with 2s-complement representation
                      (        forth.asm):02386         * for signed numbers, the way to go is to use circular arithmetic: compute
                      (        forth.asm):02387         * x=(index-limit)+minint, and observe if the addition x+n crosses the boundary
                      (        forth.asm):02388         * between minint and maxint. Many architectures report this through the
                      (        forth.asm):02389         * overflow flag."
