                      (        forth.asm):03716         * Double (numerator high/low) gets divided by a single cell number. Please note
                      (        forth.asm):03717         * that this is a strictly unsigned business. Input parameters are supposed to
                      (        forth.asm):03718         * have been set up by the caller on the system stack. The quotient (high/low)
                      (        forth.asm):03719         * and remainder are returned the same way. Current users of this routine are
                      (        forth.asm):03720         * CVT (#) and UMSLMOD (UM/MOD).
                      (        forth.asm):03721         *
                      (        forth.asm):03722         * Stack structure:
                      (        forth.asm):03723         * ,s    Return address          16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03724         * 2,s   Remainder               16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03725         * 4,s   Bitmask high            16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03726         * 6,s   Bitmask low             16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03727         * 8,s   Quotient high           16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03728         * 10,s  Quotient low            16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03729         * 12,s  Numerator high          16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03730         * 14,s  Numerator low           16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03731         * 16,s  Denominator             16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03732         * 18,s  Remainder carry         8 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03733         *
